# App Runtime

`internal/app` provides ordered startup/shutdown hooks and app-level timeout policy for application resources.

## Phases

- `BeforeStartup`
- `Startup`
- `AfterStartup`
- `BeforeShutdown`
- `Shutdown`
- `AfterShutdown`

Startup phases run in registration order.  
Shutdown phases run in reverse registration order.

## How To Register Hooks

Primary extension point: `internal/app/lifecycle_registry.go`.

That file is render-once and built by Wire, so you can inject repositories/services into `NewLifecycleRegistry(...)` and use them in `Register(...)`.

Hooks are registered on the lifecycle manager:

```go
manager.On(BeforeStartup, func(ctx context.Context) error {
	// pre-start setup
	return nil
})

manager.On(Startup, func(ctx context.Context) error {
	// start resource
	return nil
})

manager.On(Shutdown, func(ctx context.Context) error {
	// stop resource
	return nil
})
```

## Where To Register

Use `internal/app/lifecycle_registry.go`:

Example:

```go
type LifecycleRegistry struct {
	userRepo *users.UserRepo
}

func NewLifecycleRegistry(userRepo *users.UserRepo) *LifecycleRegistry {
	return &LifecycleRegistry{userRepo: userRepo}
}

func (r *LifecycleRegistry) Register(lifecycle *Lifecycle) {
	lifecycle.On(Startup, func(ctx context.Context) error {
		return r.userRepo.SeedDefaults(ctx)
	})

	lifecycle.On(Shutdown, func(ctx context.Context) error {
		return nil
	})
}
```

## Notes

- Keep hooks idempotent.
- Keep shutdown hooks fast and context-aware.
- Return errors when startup cannot continue.
- Shutdown errors are aggregated.
